      "writtenOn": "2020-09-25T23:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Kind of.  If there is a kernel bug, any pointer could potentially be NULL.  We don\u0027t put BUG_ON(NULL) before every pointer dereference.  The question is are these cases special/important enough to need it, and if so, shouldn\u0027t they be changed to WARN_ON() + recovery instead.  It wasn\u0027t immediately obvious how to recover from the two cases in trusty-ipc.c, but maybe:\n\nvds_get_txbuf():\n  if (WARN_ON(!mb))\n        return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);\n\n_handle_rxbuf():        \n  kref_put(\u0026chan-\u003erefcount, _free_chan);\n  if (WARN_ON(!rxbuf))\n        return -EINVAL;",
